Picked a nice night to come out, huh?
It's like Grand Central around here.


00:43:28.288 --> 00:43:29.880
It's been like this.


00:43:30.023 --> 00:43:34.357
I'm lucky if I get home by midnight.
It's like nothing we've seen before.


00:43:39.232 --> 00:43:41.166
Something I gotta sign?


00:43:41.267 --> 00:43:43.167
Yeah. It's right here.


00:43:43.269 --> 00:43:45.737
I'm taking this with me. I'll register
it with Essex County, all right?


00:43:45.872 --> 00:43:47.430
All right.


00:43:49.542 --> 00:43:55.174
<i>America's public enemy number one
in the United States is drug abuse.</i>


00:43:56.582 --> 00:43:58.516
<i>In order to fight and
defeat this enemy,</i>


00:43:58.618 --> 00:44:03.419
<i>it is necessary to wage a new,
all-out offensive.</i>


00:44:03.790 --> 00:44:06.452
<i>Federal authorities
have announced their intention</i>


00:44:06.592 --> 00:44:09.060
<i>to establish special
narcotics bureaus</i>


00:44:09.162 --> 00:44:11.926
<i>in Washington, New York,
Los Angeles, Chicago...</i>


00:44:12.065 --> 00:44:14.761
A detective without the
support of his fellow detectives


00:44:14.867 --> 00:44:16.858
really can't do much.


00:44:18.471 --> 00:44:20.200
You know why I don't have it.


00:44:21.307 --> 00:44:23.707
Doesn't matter.
You did what you had to do.


00:44:24.410 --> 00:44:27.937
Greatest city in the world! And
it's turning into an open sewer.


00:44:28.481 --> 00:44:31.746
Everybody's stealing, dealing.


00:44:33.186 --> 00:44:36.553
Look at you. You can't work
because you did your job.


00:44:36.656 --> 00:44:40.057
Good news is, you're not
the only honest cop in town.


00:44:40.159 --> 00:44:44.721
The special narcotics bureau in
Washington is not a dog and pony show.


00:44:44.998 --> 00:44:48.399
They are sincere. I know this because
they want us to orchestrate it.


00:44:48.501 --> 00:44:50.992
And I want you to head
up things here on our end.


00:44:51.137 --> 00:44:53.071
If it's federal, who do I
answer to, the post office?


00:44:53.206 --> 00:44:54.468
No, you answer to me,


00:44:54.607 --> 00:44:57.007
me and the US Attorney,
nobody else.


00:44:58.978 --> 00:45:01.173
You never step foot
in a police station again.


00:45:01.280 --> 00:45:04.272
You work out of your own
place, you pick your own guys,


00:45:04.384 --> 00:45:06.511
guys that you know would not
take a nickel off the sidewalk.


00:45:31.427 --> 00:45:34.760
Well, we got
the lovely transit.


00:45:36.832 --> 00:45:39.767
600-year-old
mahogany doors.


00:45:42.438 --> 00:45:45.635
Now, look at that.
Can't you just feel it?


00:45:46.308 --> 00:45:48.401
I think it's lovely.


00:45:48.511 --> 00:45:50.604
Watch your step.


00:45:54.850 --> 00:45:57.216
Look at these
beautiful floors.


00:45:57.319 --> 00:45:59.310
At least, I don't know,
200 years old.


00:45:59.422 --> 00:46:01.356
And it's hard to
