01:52:59.361 --> 01:53:00.988
This is your place?
Mmm.


01:53:01.130 --> 01:53:04.964
You know what that's worth?
Ski in, ski out. Five bedrooms.


01:53:05.100 --> 01:53:07.796
Sauna. Everything.
We were guests.


01:53:12.941 --> 01:53:14.568
It's your place.


01:53:29.691 --> 01:53:32.182
Isn't there
something we can do,


01:53:34.029 --> 01:53:36.589
about leaving
the big guy alone?


01:53:36.999 --> 01:53:38.933
You know who I mean.


01:53:39.034 --> 01:53:42.595
I don't report what you just said,
I can get in a lot of trouble.


01:53:42.704 --> 01:53:45.673
I do report it,
then the trouble is yours.


01:53:47.709 --> 01:53:50.007
I'm hoping you won't do that.


01:53:50.846 --> 01:53:53.371
Richie, come on.
I'm not taping it.


01:53:53.515 --> 01:53:56.348
How do you know?
Because we're friends.


01:53:56.685 --> 01:53:59.119
And I'm telling you,
this is a real offer.


01:53:59.221 --> 01:54:01.121
From who? Your uncle?


01:54:04.827 --> 01:54:07.318
Why would you do this? Why
would you risk our friendship?


01:54:07.429 --> 01:54:08.794
Because


01:54:11.066 --> 01:54:13.364
I care what happens to you.


01:54:15.437 --> 01:54:17.302
You shouldn't have done this.


01:54:17.406 --> 01:54:20.466
I had to, I had no choice.
Neither do you. Richie!


01:54:21.343 --> 01:54:25.143
You don't have a choice.
Just leave Frank Lucas alone.


01:54:26.849 --> 01:54:28.282
Frank Lucas?


01:54:29.518 --> 01:54:30.644
Yeah.


01:54:33.322 --> 01:54:36.189
You tell Marie I had to leave.
I'm sorry.


01:54:37.025 --> 01:54:38.492
Tell her why.


01:55:21.403 --> 01:55:22.870
Don't shoot! Don't shoot! Talk! Talk!
Don't shoot!


01:55:22.971 --> 01:55:25.269
Are you Richie Roberts?
Yes, so what?


01:55:26.208 --> 01:55:28.039
You've been served. I'm sorry.


01:55:42.791 --> 01:55:43.780
All right.


01:55:47.796 --> 01:55:48.785
Laurie.


01:55:50.933 --> 01:55:54.630
Look, I'm sorry I never gave you the
kind of life you wanted, all right.


01:55:54.770 --> 01:55:57.068
I'm sorry it was never enough.


01:56:00.175 --> 01:56:02.803
Don't punish me
for being honest.


01:56:02.945 --> 01:56:04.913
Don't take my boy away.


01:56:07.282 --> 01:56:10.615
What are you saying?
That because you were honest


01:56:10.752 --> 01:56:13.915
and you didn't take money like
every other cop, I left you?


01:56:14.022 --> 01:56:16.547
No, you don't take money
for one reason.


01:56:16.658 --> 01:56:19.456
To buy being dishonest
about everything else.


01:56:19.962 --> 01:56:21.953
And that's worse than taking
money nobody gives a shit about.


01:56:22.097 --> 01:56:25.066
Drug money, gambling money
nobody's gonna miss.


01:56:25.467 --> 01:56:28.925
You know, I'd rather you took
it and been honest with me.


01:56:29.037 --> 01:56:31.733
Or don't take it. I don't care.
But then don't go cheat on me.


01:56:31.840 --> 01:56:34.934
Don't cheat on your kid by never
being around. Don't go out and get laid


01:56:35.043 --> 01:56:37.978
by your snitches and your
secretaries and strippers!


01:56:38.113 --> 01:56:40.843
I can tell by just looking,
she's one of them.


01:56:40.983 --> 01:56:41.972
You...


01:56:42.284 --> 01:56:46.584
You think you're going to heaven
because you're honest, but you're not.


01:56:46.989 --> 01:56:49.583
You're going to the same hell as
the crooked cops you can't stand.


01:56:50.859 --> 01:56:52.417
All rise.


01:56:56.832 --> 01:56:58.823
Please be seated.


01:57:00.002 --> 01:57:01.697
Miss Dickerson,


01:57:01.837 --> 01:57:04.328
before the court
renders its opinion,


01:57:04.473 --> 01:57:07.135
is there anything else
you'd like to be heard on?


01:57:07.242 --> 01:57:08.971
Yes, Your Honor.


01:57:09.077 --> 01:57:12.205
Your Honor, a lot has been said
here today about how unsavory


01:57:12.347 --> 01:57:16.306
Mr. Roberts' environment is for
a child. How dangerous it is.


01:57:16.418 --> 01:57:20.184
We tell him to protect us. We
give him that responsibility,


01:57:20.322 --> 01:57:22.847
but then say, "Oh, we don't
trust you to raise a child.


01:57:22.991 --> 01:57:24.515
"We don't think
you're fit for that. "


01:57:24.626 --> 01:57:26.218
I'm not.


01:57:27.029 --> 01:57:28.496
You're right.


01:57:29.698 --> 01:57:32.132
Being around me
is no place for a kid.


01:57:32.234 --> 01:57:35.465
You take him to Vegas.
I'll come see him when I can.


01:57:38.407 --> 01:57:42.036
Your Honor, I want to apologize
for wasting the court's time.


01:57:53.922 --> 01:57:55.617
Doc.


01:57:55.724 --> 01:57:57.123
I see them.


01:57:57.225 --> 01:57:58.715
There he is.


01:58:17.245 --> 01:58:18.872
The fuck is this guy doing?


01:58:19.648 --> 01:58:20.979
Hey!
Champagne.


01:58:21.083 --> 01:58:23.278
Merry Christmas, Detectives. For us?


01:58:23.385 --> 01:58:25.216
Yeah. Enjoy that.


01:58:25.587 --> 01:58:27.919
You fellas have a good time.
Mmm-hmm.


01:58:29.324 --> 01:58:30.882
It's Cristal.


01:58:34.730 --> 01:58:37.028
<i>South Vietnamese
troops called in air strikes</i>


01:58:37.132 --> 01:58:40.067
<i>on Communist positions
inside the city.</i>


01:58:41.570 --> 01:58:44.266
Paying off Johnny Law,
that's one thing.


01:58:44.373 --> 01:58:45.965
There ain't no problem
with that.


01:58:46.074 --> 01:58:48.770
I've been paying off the
police since I was 10 years old.


01:58:48.877 --> 01:58:51.539
Put more of their kids through
college than the National Merit Award.


01:58:51.680 --> 01:58:53.443
Give me one of
them round one... Yeah.


01:58:53.548 --> 01:58:55.482
This is different,
though. These...


01:58:55.584 --> 01:58:59.486
Special Investigative Unit. That's their
problem. They think they're special.


01:58:59.588 --> 01:59:02.216
Fucking crooks.
No code of ethics.


01:59:02.357 --> 01:59:03.381
What do you think?


01:59:03.492 --> 01:59:05.619
Looks great. It's beautiful.


01:59:05.927 --> 01:59:07.053
Good.


01:59:07.662 --> 01:59:09.721
The police, that ain't the
only somebody I'm worried about.


01:59:09.831 --> 01:59:12.800
I seeing cars where I ain't never
seen them before, people I don't know.


01:59:12.934 --> 01:59:13.901
Yeah, me, too.


01:59:14.002 --> 01:59:14.764
Ho, ho, ho.


01:59:17.589 --> 01:59:18.783
Merry Christmas,
Charlie.


01:59:18.890 --> 01:59:19.982
Thank you.


01:59:20.091 --> 01:59:21.353
I love you.


01:59:21.526 --> 01:59:22.823
I love you, too.


01:59:24.329 --> 01:59:26.160
Here, take this.


01:59:26.431 --> 01:59:28.126
A quick toast,
and then I'll be off.


01:59:28.466 --> 01:59:30.798
<i>What happened here
was an accident of war.</i>


01:59:30.969 --> 01:59:33.335
<i>Somebody made a mistake.</i>


01:59:34.339 --> 01:59:36.534
Bumpy ain't hardly
ever go out no more.


01:59:36.708 --> 01:59:38.938
After a certain point
he stayed in the house.


01:59:41.713 --> 01:59:43.874
Watch TV.


01:59:45.183 --> 01:59:47.151
Play chess.
Read the newspaper.


01:59:48.820 --> 01:59:50.913
I though he was just trying
to lead the quiet life,


01:59:51.022 --> 01:59:53.081
but no, he couldn't
go nowhere.


01:59:53.191 --> 01:59:54.658
Not without
something happening.


01:59:54.826 --> 01:59:56.316
Frankie...


01:59:56.494 --> 01:59:58.086
We can still go out.


01:59:58.263 --> 01:59:59.890
With who? Where?


01:59:59.998 --> 02:00:01.625
Well, with...


02:00:01.799 --> 02:00:03.391
But I know he's
under surveillance.


02:00:04.569 --> 02:00:06.230
Ain't gonna be
no Christmas time


02:00:06.404 --> 02:00:08.133
with my family
being here no more.


02:00:08.239 --> 02:00:11.367
Why don't you just pay
who you have to pay?


02:00:11.476 --> 02:00:13.569
I do pay them. I pay
thousands and millions


02:00:13.745 --> 02:00:15.838
to dope dealers,
crooks, cops.


02:00:16.314 --> 02:00:17.372
I pay everybody.


02:00:17.548 --> 02:00:18.640
I pay more than
they should get.


02:00:18.750 --> 02:00:20.911
I can't satisfy
nobody!


02:00:21.019 --> 02:00:23.078
It's like dope! Everybody's strung out!


02:00:23.187 --> 02:00:25.212
The more you give 'em,
the more they want.


02:00:25.356 --> 02:00:27.654
They expect more.


02:00:28.660 --> 02:00:30.855
Give more and they want more.


02:00:35.566 --> 02:00:37.659
Do you want to go out?


02:00:38.603 --> 02:00:40.571
All right, baby. Put
something of what you got.


02:00:40.672 --> 02:00:41.866
Should I?
Yeah.


02:00:41.973 --> 02:00:43.167
That's Christmas spirit.


02:00:43.274 --> 02:00:45.504
<i>That's what I'm talking about.
Feliz Navidad.</i>


02:00:45.610 --> 02:00:47.339
Something nice?
Mmm-hmm.


02:00:55.086 --> 02:00:56.417
We're going to
have a great time.


02:00:56.521 --> 02:00:57.613
<i>That's right, chica.</i>


02:00:57.722 --> 02:01:00.282
Mr. Lucas.
Enjoy your evening.


02:01:01.326 --> 02:01:02.884
It's all clear.


02:01:07.247 --> 02:01:07.975
Nicky!


02:01:08.081 --> 02:01:09.878
Who is that? There's
your boy, Nicky. See him?


02:01:09.983 --> 02:01:10.972
Know what I'm saying?


02:01:11.084 --> 02:01:13.678
Yeah, I see him.
Let's keep going.


02:01:14.421 --> 02:01:15.479
Around back?


02:01:15.589 --> 02:01:18.683
Hell, no. I ain't
sneaking into my own club.


02:01:19.092 --> 02:01:21.026
Incredible.
Huh?


02:01:43.283 --> 02:01:44.682
Come on.


02:01:47.554 --> 02:01:48.578
Hold on. Hold on.


02:01:57.030 --> 02:01:58.054
What?


02:01:58.198 --> 02:01:59.995
I want to wait in the car.


02:02:00.100 --> 02:02:03.160
Frank, I got it. I got it.
I'll wait for it. I got it.


02:02:03.570 --> 02:02:05.595
Get that yellow sauce.
Yellow sauce.


02:02:05.739 --> 02:02:07.764
And the chicken.
The Kung Pao chicken.


02:02:14.047 --> 02:02:15.776
Can you turn the heater on?


02:02:22.122 --> 02:02:24.283
Shit. I'm gonna go
get the keys.


02:02:38.238 --> 02:02:40.763
Doc, give me the keys.
Here you go.


02:02:46.513 --> 02:02:47.775
Doc!


02:02:51.918 --> 02:02:53.715
Get out of the car.


02:03:00.160 --> 02:03:02.094
You okay?
Yeah.


02:03:02.195 --> 02:03:03.253
Shit.


02:03:03.363 --> 02:03:04.455
Come on.


02:03:04.598 --> 02:03:06.623
Come on, baby. You all right?


02:03:07.601 --> 02:03:08.898
Let's go.


02:03:29.556 --> 02:03:31.023
Was it Nicky?


02:03:32.693 --> 02:03:35.025
We'll go right now and fucking
kill him whether it was him or not,


02:03:35.162 --> 02:03:37.096
you say the word, Frankie.


02:03:38.632 --> 02:03:40.964
We got to do something, Frank.


02:03:41.401 --> 02:03:42.425
We can't just sit here.


02:03:42.536 --> 02:03:44.026
We're leaving.


02:03:47.174 --> 02:03:48.835
All right, everybody get out.
You all right, man?


02:03:48.975 --> 02:03:51.102
Go on home. It's Christmas time.
Go and be with your families.


02:03:51.211 --> 02:03:52.508
I'm all right.


02:03:52.646 --> 02:03:55.547
Go on. Go ahead.
Be with your kids.


02:03:55.682 --> 02:03:56.979
Go ahead.


02:04:09.162 --> 02:04:10.220
Where are we gonna go, huh?


02:04:10.364 --> 02:04:11.956
We're gonna go to Spain,
somewhere? China?


02:04:12.065 --> 02:04:15.557
Huh? Come on, sit down.
Tell me where you want to go.


02:04:16.236 --> 02:04:19.171
Frank, we can go
anywhere we want.


02:04:19.272 --> 02:04:21.172
No, we can't.
We can live anywhere, Frank.


02:04:21.274 --> 02:04:22.969
Where? And do what?
Run? Hide?


02:04:23.076 --> 02:04:26.011
Frank Lucas don't run
from nobody, baby.


02:04:26.113 --> 02:04:27.910
We ain't going nowhere.
We're gonna stay right here.


02:04:28.048 --> 02:04:30.312
We're gonna stay right here.
This is my home.


02:04:30.417 --> 02:04:33.716
This is where my business is,
my wife, my mother, my family.


02:04:33.854 --> 02:04:36.322
My country.
I ain't going nowhere.


02:04:37.023 --> 02:04:39.218
I ain't running from nobody!


02:04:40.594 --> 02:04:42.221
This is America.


02:04:49.035 --> 02:04:51.595
And you ain't going
nowhere, either!


02:04:53.640 --> 02:04:54.766
Huh?


02:04:57.077 --> 02:04:59.739
<i>A ceasefire, internationally
supervised, will begin</i>


02:04:59.880 --> 02:05:04.180
<i>at 7:00 p. m. this Saturday,
January 27th, Washington time.</i>


02:05:04.284 --> 02:05:06.309
I'll call you back.


02:05:06.586 --> 02:05:08.816
Hey! What are you doing?


02:05:11.024 --> 02:05:12.218
Richie.


02:05:16.062 --> 02:05:17.154
Wow.


02:05:19.433 --> 02:05:24.234
So, what I hear it was the
Corsican mob took a shot at Frank.


02:05:24.371 --> 02:05:26.202
You know, French Connection,
Fernando Rey,


02:05:26.306 --> 02:05:28.672
the exporters that
Frank has put out of business.


02:05:30.076 --> 02:05:32.203
Look, I can take care
of him in New York.


02:05:32.312 --> 02:05:33.779
I just don't want to have
to worry that every time


02:05:33.914 --> 02:05:35.381
he drives across
the bridge to Jersey,


02:05:35.482 --> 02:05:38.280
someone's gonna take
another shot at him.


02:05:38.418 --> 02:05:41.683
Richie, you and I gotta
start working together.


02:05:42.155 --> 02:05:44.521
We need to step up
our efforts.


02:05:44.891 --> 02:05:47.553
Next time,
their aim could be better.


02:05:48.161 --> 02:05:50.755
We need to keep
this cash cow alive.


02:05:56.603 --> 02:05:58.798
What the fuck
are you doing here?


02:05:59.306 --> 02:06:00.637
Whoa!


02:06:03.844 --> 02:06:07.780
Were you actually gonna arrest Frank
Lucas? What's the matter with you?


02:06:08.181 --> 02:06:10.376
What, you don't know?
No.


02:06:11.084 --> 02:06:13.609
Everybody in New Jersey's crazy. Oh.


02:06:14.154 --> 02:06:17.590
You know what we do here?
Cops arrest bad guys.


02:06:19.826 --> 02:06:21.817
Before you get on
that bridge again,


02:06:21.962 --> 02:06:25.329
you should call me first,
just make sure it's safe.


02:06:28.535 --> 02:06:32.130
"I'm more enlightened than some of my
friends. I can guarantee you peace of mind. "


02:06:32.272 --> 02:06:34.570
That's what you
told me, Dominic.


02:06:35.842 --> 02:06:38.402
"I can guarantee you
peace of mind!"


02:06:38.512 --> 02:06:40.571
I don't feel so peaceful!


02:06:42.048 --> 02:06:43.174
Huh?


02:06:45.619 --> 02:06:47.814
They tried to kill my wife!


02:06:52.225 --> 02:06:53.783
Who was that? Huh?


02:06:55.996 --> 02:06:58.362
Maybe it was one
of your peoples.


02:06:58.498 --> 02:07:00.693
I don't know yet. No.
You don't know?


02:07:00.834 --> 02:07:02.358
You don't know.


02:07:03.737 --> 02:07:06.672
I'll tell you what I know.
Maybe I should just put 500 guns


02:07:06.806 --> 02:07:08.865
out there on the street and just
start shooting up some people,


02:07:08.975 --> 02:07:09.964
just to make a point.


02:07:10.076 --> 02:07:13.375
Frank, it was a junkie. It
was a rival. Some dumb-ass kid


02:07:13.513 --> 02:07:17.210
trying to make a name for himself.
Somebody you forgot to pay off.


02:07:17.350 --> 02:07:20.285
Someone you slighted
without even realizing it.


02:07:20.387 --> 02:07:24.653
Could be someone you put out of business
from being so successful. Look at you.


02:07:25.492 --> 02:07:29.053
Success, it's got enemies,
Frank. Lots of enemies.


02:07:30.697 --> 02:07:33.222
So your success took a shot at
you. What are you gonna do now?


02:07:33.366 --> 02:07:37.029
How you gonna kill it? You're
gonna become unsuccessful?


02:07:38.004 --> 02:07:40.837
Frank, we can be successful
and have enemies, right?


02:07:41.241 --> 02:07:44.506
Or we can be unsuccessful, too,
you know, we can have friends.


02:07:45.412 --> 02:07:47.505
That's the choice we make.


02:07:48.915 --> 02:07:52.544
<i>The final evacuation of
military and diplomatic personnel</i>


02:07:52.686 --> 02:07:57.055
<i>continued throughout the night, as North
Vietnamese troops marched on Saigon.</i>


02:07:57.390 --> 02:08:02.521
<i>The imminent fall of the city has brought
chaos and a growing sense of desperation.</i>


02:08:11.538 --> 02:08:14.939
international.


02:08:15.075 --> 02:08:16.599
<i>One moment, please.</i>


02:08:24.985 --> 02:08:26.350
<i>Yeah, Nate.</i>


02:08:26.453 --> 02:08:28.114
Hey, Frank. What's up, baby?


02:08:28.254 --> 02:08:29.619
What's going on over there?


02:08:29.723 --> 02:08:30.917
<i>It's all over.</i>


02:08:31.057 --> 02:08:32.888
Yeah, I'm watching the news.
What the hell's going on?


02:08:32.993 --> 02:08:34.688
<i>The game's over, Frank.</i>


02:08:34.794 --> 02:08:36.125
Huh?
It's done.


02:08:36.262 --> 02:08:38.230
Everybody going home, baby.
Give peace a chance.


02:08:38.331 --> 02:08:39.696
<i>Well, look, I'm not...
Listen to me.</i>


02:08:39.799 --> 02:08:41.357
I want two...


02:08:42.335 --> 02:08:45.133
I want 2,000
keys in the air.


02:08:45.271 --> 02:08:48.536
<i>It's impossible, Frank. All our
resources are going home. It's over.</i>


02:08:48.642 --> 02:08:50.405
I'll tell you what.
I'm on my way over there.


02:08:50.510 --> 02:08:52.444
<i>Right now? Oh, come...
Yeah.</i>


02:08:59.819 --> 02:09:01.980
You stole my shit?


02:09:02.122 --> 02:09:04.215
Spearman, wake the fuck up, man. What?


02:09:06.159 --> 02:09:07.717
Where's my shit, Darlynn?


02:09:07.827 --> 02:09:09.795
Don't hurt me, Jimmy!


02:09:11.431 --> 02:09:13.262
Jesus! What the... Police! Police!


02:09:13.366 --> 02:09:15.163
Drop the gun, Jimmy!
Drop the gun!


02:09:15.301 --> 02:09:17.496
Let me see your hands!
Jimmy, drop the fucking gun!


02:09:17.637 --> 02:09:20.401
I'm not playing with you, Jimmy!
I'll blast your fucking head off!


02:09:20.507 --> 02:09:22.304
Don't shoot! Don't shoot!


02:09:24.044 --> 02:09:27.138
I got your gun
and I got your prints.


02:09:28.448 --> 02:09:31.645
You know what you got?
You got attempted murder.


02:09:32.852 --> 02:09:34.752
Fifteen fucking years!


02:09:35.155 --> 02:09:38.488
Attempted murder is the same as
Murder One, that's a grand jury.


02:09:38.625 --> 02:09:40.855
Now, a grand jury could
come back favorably.


02:09:40.994 --> 02:09:44.088
It could be reduced
to manslaughter.


02:09:44.197 --> 02:09:46.358
All right?
Maybe even self-defense.


02:09:46.499 --> 02:09:48.330
It all just depends
on how we wanna deal with you.


02:09:48.468 --> 02:09:50.436
See where this is
fucking going, Jimmy?


02:09:50.537 --> 02:09:53.995
Let's say you beat it. What you think
your cousin Frank is gonna think?


02:09:54.140 --> 02:09:56.472
Right, he is gonna know,
at some point in time,


02:09:56.576 --> 02:09:59.044
we sat you down, and we
talked to you like this.


02:09:59.179 --> 02:10:01.841
And then you go to court
and you beat attempted murder?


02:10:01.981 --> 02:10:05.439
